p.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,allow_unicode=True,width=100))
notes=p.parent/'ptsH-notes.md';assert not notes.exists()
notes.write_text('''# Bacillus subtilis ptsH review notes\n\n## 2026-11-07\n\nP08877/BSU13900 is the native carbohydrate HPr of strain 168. UniProt records its membership in PTHR33705:SF2 (official label PHOSPHOCARRIER PROTEIN NPR), but the curated native function is enzyme I → HPr → sugar-specific EIIA. This is a positive functional counterexample to assigning a nitrogen-regulatory relay solely from that subfamily name. It does not imply that every member of the subfamily is a carbohydrate carrier.\n\nThe two core activities use distinct phosphosites. His15 participates in phosphoryl transfer; Ser46 phosphorylation controls association with CcpA. PMID:1549615 provides native structural evidence and proposes transfer geometry, while PMID:8596444 directly reports purified-complex DNA footprinting. PMID:8195089 adds mutation/reversion evidence for regulation of carbohydrate utilization. The current accessible caches of these papers are abstract-only; no unseen kinetic data or detailed assay conditions are inferred.\n\nAll five seeded rows, qualifiers and supporting entities are preserved. Both bare protein-binding rows are removed under the specific repository policy, without denying the underlying associations. No NEW annotation rows are added. Core molecular functions are independently supported syntheses; the reviewed process terms were already present. The IBA is judged against native function, not donor count. No PAINT gain/loss placement is asserted.\n\nOfficial current GO definitions were checked for GO:0016775 and GO:0003714. The latter allows a cofactor binding a DNA-bound transcription factor; chromatin remodeling is a common example, not a requirement that excludes this bacterial mechanism. Cytoplasm is retained because the available localization source does not resolve a finer anatomical site.\n\nThe shared Falcon module-research attempt failed provider authentication (HTTP 403); direct primary-source assessment was used. No provider-generated report was fabricated.\n''')
(c/'BACSU-ptsH-preservation.json').write_text(json.dumps({'original_rows':5,'current_rows':5,'new_rows':0,'original_payloads_unchanged':baseline==[payload(a) for a in d['existing_annotations']],'raw_files':raw,'core_functions':2,'focused_validation':'pending'},indent=2)+'\n')
print('BACSU ptsH reviewed:5 rows preserved,2 core functions,0 NEW rows')
